[size=4][b]Description[/b][/size]
Spend less time hauling resources and more time exploring. Improved Lodge Storage makes the Lodge's unlimited storage convenient to use, connects it to the basement's crafting stations, and adds storage access at the New Atlantis Spaceport and wherever you build a home.

[size=4][b]One inventory, multiple access points[/b][/size]
Your Lodge storage is available in three convenient locations:
[list]
[*][b]Lodge bedroom:[/b] a safe in its familiar location.[/*]
[*][b]Lodge basement:[/b] a wall-mounted Captain's Locker beside the crafting area.[/*]
[*][b]New Atlantis Spaceport:[/b] a large industrial cargo container near the Trade Authority kiosk, so you can unload before heading into town.[/*]
[/list]
Every Lodge Storage access point opens the same unlimited inventory: the original safe in your Lodge bedroom. Deposit items at the spaceport and use them downstairs, or retrieve them from your own home. Items already in the bedroom safe are available immediately.

[size=4][b]Craft directly from Lodge storage[/b][/size]
All six crafting and research stations in the Lodge basement can use resources from your Lodge storage, alongside your personal inventory and the game's normal access to ship cargo. Keep your materials in the safe and craft without carrying them around.

[size=4][b]Ship cargo in the basement[/b][/size]
A blue [b]Ship Cargo[/b] panel beside the basement locker opens your current home ship's cargo hold. Transfer supplies between your ship, your inventory, and Lodge storage without leaving the crafting area. The panel automatically follows your choice of home ship.

[size=4][b]Build storage access in your homes and outposts[/b][/size]
Two wall-mounted devices are available under [b]Misc[/b] in the build menu for outposts and player homes:
[list]
[*][b]Lodge Storage:[/b] a Captain's Locker that opens your shared Lodge inventory.[/*]
[*][b]Ship Cargo:[/b] a blue cargo panel that opens your current home ship's cargo hold.[/*]
[/list]
Both are free to build and require no research or perks. Place, move, and remove them through the normal build menu. Removing an access point does not remove any stored items.

[size=4][b]Installation instructions[/b][/size]
[list=1]
[*]Install the downloaded archive with your mod manager.[/*]
[*]Enable [b]ImprovedLodgeStorage.esm[/b].[/*]
[*]Restart Starfield.[/*]
[/list]
For manual installation, extract the archive into Starfield's [b]Data[/b] folder and enable [b]ImprovedLodgeStorage.esm[/b] in your plugin list.

[size=4][b]Compatibility[/b][/size]
Mods that replace the Lodge bedroom safe or change the same basement workbenches' storage links may require a compatibility patch.

[size=4][b]Uninstall[/b][/size]
Disable the mod in your mod manager and restart Starfield. Your items remain in the original Lodge bedroom safe and are still accessible there. The added containers are access points to existing inventories, so you do not need to empty them before uninstalling.

[size=4][b]Source code[/b][/size]
Source code and build instructions: [url=https://github.com/kayahr/ImprovedLodgeStorage]https://github.com/kayahr/ImprovedLodgeStorage[/url]
